{"availability":"available","full":"drkokorev/Planly","name":"Planly","description":"Minimalist day planner PWA. Vertical timeline with drag-to-reschedule, repeating tasks, month calendar, tasks in folders, formatted notes, archive. No accounts, offline-first, optional sync between devices via a single access code (Cloudflare Pages + KV or self-hosted). One HTML file, six languages.","category":"Productivity","language":"HTML","stars":4,"forks":1,"created":"2026-09-18T07:36:55Z","updated":"2026-10-04T20:26:23Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://planly.site","topics":[],"demo":"https://planly.site/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T16:23:52.534Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T16:23:52.534Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T16:23:52.534Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T16:23:52.534Z","stars":4,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A minimalist day planner that lives in your browser. One HTML file, no framework, no accounts, no server required. Works offline, installs to the home screen, and syncs between devices through a single access code when you want it to.","Everything lives in the browser's storage on your device. The server, when you use one, holds a single JSON document per access code and knows nothing else.","The demo's sync is invite-only (it's the author's instance); deploy your own in five minutes — see below."],"features":["Day — a vertical timeline where each task is a block as tall as its duration. Tap a time to add, drag to move, pull the bottom edge to resize. Overlaps split into columns. A list view shows the same day as rows with…","Repeats — every day or chosen weekdays. Edits apply to one day; \"apply to all future\" pushes them down the series.","Calendar — tap the date to open a month view; days with tasks are underlined.","Tasks — things without a time, in folders you create, with four priorities; the top one, Urgent, frames the task in bright red wherever it appears. Deleting a non-empty folder asks whether to keep its tasks in the main…","Notes — drafts by topic with headings, bullet and numbered lists, bold and italic. Saves as you type."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/drkokorev/Planly/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a2f8585e85f2b3c1e484821408422d120c0dd15c27ed41dce3c5c28c17001790","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T16:23:52.645Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T16:23:52.645Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A minimalist day planner that lives in your browser. One HTML file, no framework, no accounts, no server required. Works offline, installs to the home screen, and syncs between devices through a single access code when you want it to.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/drkokorev/Planly/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"not_required","text":"One HTML file, no framework, no accounts, no server required.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/drkokorev/Planly/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"You need a Cloudflare account and Node.js 18+.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/drkokorev/Planly/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"a2f8585e85f2b3c1e484821408422d120c0dd15c27ed41dce3c5c28c17001790","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/drkokorev/Planly/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T16:23:52.646Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-04T20:26:23Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/drkokorev/Planly/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T16:23:52.647Z","hash":"a2f8585e85f2b3c1e484821408422d120c0dd15c27ed41dce3c5c28c17001790","originalBytes":13262,"storedBytes":13262,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["app","sync","one","day","server","code","pages","data","planly","tasks","task","api","bash","static","time","any","cloudflare","docker","free","add","build","copy","days","every","folder","list","offline","only","per","same","wrangler","codes","create","file","index.html","note","src","ve